    "result_text": "The repository has a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**What the change does:** on a successful owner create, an audit line is emitted via the SLF4J logger named `AUDIT` containing the owner id, customerCode and registrationDate.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **New step `AuditOwnerCreated`** (`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`) \u2014 reads the stored `@Val Owner` and logs to `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`:\n   ```\n   Created owner id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\n   ```\n\n2. **Wired into the pipeline** (`src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 inserted between `save` and `respond` so the owner's generated id, customerCode and (business-day-adjusted) registrationDate are all populated when it runs:\n   ```\n   save \u2192 audit \u2192 respond\n   ```\n\nI placed it after `save` deliberately: the owner id only exists once persisted, and the step carries the same `transaction` governance as its neighbors so it stays inside the request's single commit.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` (which captures the `AUDIT` logger and asserts the line contains the id, customerCode and registrationDate) passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS` (1 test, 0 failures). The captured log line confirms it, e.g. `AUDIT - Created owner id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-04`.",
